<title>FRANCE: Seagram sells Heidsieck Monopole - paper.</title>
<headline>Seagram sells Heidsieck Monopole - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian beverage firm Seagram Co. Ltd has finalised the sale of the champagne brand Heidsieck Monopole to the Vranken group, Le Figaro said on Friday.</p>
<p>Heidsieck Monopole belonged to the French Mumm house, a subsidiary of Seagram. The amount of the transaction was not disclosed.</p>
<p>Mumm's management told the French daily the sale of the Heidsieck Monopole name, the stock, and some 132 hectares of vineyards was made at a &quot;market price&quot;.</p>
<p>Last year Heidsieck Monopole sold some 1.2 million bottles of champagne.</p>
</text>
